/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2253508830","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453#issuecomment-2253508830","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453","id":2253508830,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86GUdDe","user":{"login":"thedavidmeister","id":629710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTcxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/629710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister","html_url":"https://github.com/thedavidmeister","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-07-26T21:09:03Z","updated_at":"2024-07-26T21:09:03Z","body":"@jlovejoy i'm going off the wording here:\r\n\r\n> For new licenses, there are definitive plans for the license to be used in one or a few significant projects.\r\n\r\nThe definitive plans are that I will personally update all the contracts as soon as it lands in SPDX.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2253508830/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2371402344","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453#issuecomment-2371402344","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453","id":2371402344,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86NWLpo","user":{"login":"thedavidmeister","id":629710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTcxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/629710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister","html_url":"https://github.com/thedavidmeister","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-24T14:06:12Z","updated_at":"2024-09-24T14:06:12Z","body":"hey @jlovejoy looking for some guidance here\r\n\r\ni'm reasonably sure that i'll break tooling if i go ahead and reference a license that isn't included yet\r\n\r\ndefinitely qualify for \"definitive plans\" for use as our lawyer is regularly reminding me to update :)\r\n\r\nif you need some kind of inclusion of the license before it enters SPDX, what would that look like? i could update a LICENSE.txt or something if that helps?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2371402344/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2377440327","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453#issuecomment-2377440327","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453","id":2377440327,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86NtNxH","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-26T16:35:50Z","updated_at":"2024-09-26T16:35:50Z","body":"Summary of discussion on 9/26 legal call:\r\nSeems like inclusion on the SPDX License List (based on the inclusion principles) is getting conflated with the need/desire for an SPDX license id and ability to use that to identify the license.  \r\n\r\nTaking the first question of inclusion: This license has a couple issues in terms of meeting those - 1) it's not a open source license/doesn't meet those definitions b/c it has a restriction on use; and 2) it sounds like one project is planning to use and this is a new project, so \"significance\" and \"substantial\" is still TBD.  \r\n\r\nHowever, not being accepted for the SPDX License List does not mean you can't use a valid SPDX id. We have `LicenseRef-<name>` for just this purpose, so we'd recommend going that route. \r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2377440327/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2377486361","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453#issuecomment-2377486361","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453","id":2377486361,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86NtZAZ","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-09-26T17:01:28Z","updated_at":"2024-09-26T17:01:28Z","body":"Looking at this one through the lens of the \"Other factors\" in the SPDX [License Inclusion Principles](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/blob/main/DOCS/license-inclusion-principles.md):\r\n\r\n* I don't think this is likely to be considered as satisfying the OSD. Specifically, section 4.3 appears to impose restrictions on particular use cases of the software.\r\n* Where a license doesn't satisfy \"Other factor\" 1, we usually require a much higher showing for the other factors. In particular, needing to show \"Other factor\" 3 that there's very substantial use of the license in the wild.\r\n* Here, in all honesty, I don't think that the proposed project here on its own meets this threshold. I'm sure that rainlang is an interesting project and I hope it grows in significance! But for other software licenses that fall into the \"not OSD compliant\" bucket, we usually require a much stronger showing of usage in order to balance the other factors.\r\n\r\nIn light of this, I agree I wouldn't be inclined to add this to the list in its present state. If there were much broader usage (now or in the future), I might view it differently.\r\n\r\nAll that said, I would also echo @jlovejoy's point above that the `LicenseRef-` mechanism enables creating a custom SPDX-compliant license ID for licenses that aren't on the official list. Happy to provide a link to more details for that if helpful.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2377486361/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2413481752","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453#issuecomment-2413481752","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453","id":2413481752,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86P2s8Y","user":{"login":"thedavidmeister","id":629710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTcxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/629710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister","html_url":"https://github.com/thedavidmeister","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-15T10:16:31Z","updated_at":"2024-10-15T10:19:57Z","body":"@swinslow it meets the definition of open here https://opendefinition.org/od/2.1/en/\r\n\r\nthe \"restriction\" is that cryptographic private keys must remain private, it's not much of a restriction in context of web3 which is what the license is designed for, and it doesn't make the code \"closed source\" under any layman definition\r\n\r\nthe reason that is there, is to make sure that not only the code is open source, but any web3 assets that might interface with the code remain \"open assets\" as well (i.e. not your keys, not your coins)\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2413481752/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2413498223","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453#issuecomment-2413498223","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453","id":2413498223,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86P2w9v","user":{"login":"thedavidmeister","id":629710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTcxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/629710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister","html_url":"https://github.com/thedavidmeister","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-15T10:24:36Z","updated_at":"2024-10-15T10:28:04Z","body":"@swinslow when you accepted CAL, that was based only on holo/holochain, which at the time was still essentially a draft technologically and the only adoption was fundraising\r\n\r\ni know because i was a core developer on holochain at the time\r\n\r\nrainlang is in production, and raindex has about $1.5M total vol, with about $2.5k daily trading volume currently, and is growing, on track for $10k daily by end of year.\r\n\r\ndecentralicense is a much smaller thing than CAL was, as it is simply extending CAL to add some definitions, while rainlang/raindex is objectively further along now in terms of project maturity than holochain was when CAL was approved.\r\n\r\nadditionally https://cyclo.finance/ will be released under decentralicense when it will go live, which has significant capital committed already for liquidity provisions","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2413498223/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2413684104","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453#issuecomment-2413684104","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453","id":2413684104,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86P3eWI","user":{"login":"thedavidmeister","id":629710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTcxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/629710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister","html_url":"https://github.com/thedavidmeister","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-15T11:43:58Z","updated_at":"2024-10-15T11:43:58Z","body":"@jlovejoy thanks for the advice, i'm going to try it","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2413684104/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2414011521","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453#issuecomment-2414011521","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453","id":2414011521,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86P4uSB","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-15T14:02:24Z","updated_at":"2024-10-15T14:02:24Z","body":"[CAL-1.0](https://spdx.org/licenses/CAL-1.0.html) was added to the SPDX License List because it was approved by OSI. Under the [license inclusion principles](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/blob/main/DOCS/license-inclusion-principles.md), any OSI-approved license gets added to the SPDX list. That's as far as the analysis goes for CAL-1.0 (see https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/953#issuecomment-585893132 regarding this).\r\n\r\nIf DCL were to be approved by the OSI, that would be the end of the discussion and it would get added here. Since it isn't, the rest of the analysis applies.\r\n\r\nRegarding the [Open Definition](https://opendefinition.org/od/2.1/en/), I'm not convinced DCL would satisfy it either, specifically section 2.1.8:\r\n\r\n> 2.1.8 APPLICATION TO ANY PURPOSE\r\n> The license must allow use, redistribution, modification, and compilation for any purpose. The license must not restrict anyone from making use of the work in a specific field of endeavor.\r\n\r\nWhich seems to me to be a problem for section 4.3 of DCL, as it appears to impose restrictions on particular use cases of the software. In my mind, this is largely equivalent to section 6 of the [OSI Open Source Definition](https://opensource.org/osd).\r\n\r\nI don't have enough background in cryptocurrency (and don't have any intention of learning more!) to evaluate whether this is a \"significant\" project in that space.\r\n\r\nI've shared my thoughts above regarding what appears to be the usage based on e.g. the GitHub repos, and I continue to think that this license doesn't meet the mix of \"Other factors\" to warrant adding to the list at this time. If other SPDX legal team participants have a different view, please feel free to weigh in, but I'm -1 on adding unless / until there is _substantially_ greater usage in practice.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2414011521/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2419068202","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453#issuecomment-2419068202","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453","id":2419068202,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86QMA0q","user":{"login":"thedavidmeister","id":629710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTcxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/629710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister","html_url":"https://github.com/thedavidmeister","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thedavidmeister/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-17T09:47:32Z","updated_at":"2024-10-17T09:47:32Z","body":"@swinslow yes, the restriction being that the useage must be decentralised... which is basically the hardware/data equivalent of open software...\r\n\r\nimo it's strange that you believe the restriction that code must be open is :+1: for a definition of \"open\" but the restriction that data/infrastructure must be open is a :-1: for \"open\"","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2419068202/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2438389774","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453#issuecomment-2438389774","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2453","id":2438389774,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE86RVuAO","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-25T17:19:18Z","updated_at":"2024-10-25T17:19:18Z","body":"This has been discussed on (at least) two prior SPDX legal team calls, with the view being that DCL-1.0 does not meet the License Inclusion Principles at this time. Apologies if prior comments were not clear enough, but given the discussions and the comments throughout this thread, I'm going to go ahead and close this issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/2438389774/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]